### product-service API — Phase 1
#
# Runnable from IntelliJ (built in) or VS Code with the REST Client extension: click
# "Send Request" above any block. Equivalent curl commands are in docs/PHASE-1.md.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   docker compose up -d          from the repository root, starts product-db
#   ./mvnw spring-boot:run        from product-service/

@host = http://localhost:8081

### Liveness — no database involved
GET {{host}}/api/products/ping

### Health — note the "db" component, which runs a real query against Postgres
GET {{host}}/actuator/health

### List all products (the 5 rows seeded by V2__seed_products.sql)
GET {{host}}/api/products

### Get one by internal id
GET {{host}}/api/products/1

### Get one by SKU — the lookup other services will use from Phase 3
GET {{host}}/api/products/sku/IPHONE-15

### Create a product → expect 201 and a Location header
POST {{host}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "GALAXY-S25",
  "name": "Samsung Galaxy S25",
  "description": "Android smartphone, 256GB",
  "price": 74999.00
}

### Update it → PUT replaces the mutable fields wholesale
PUT {{host}}/api/products/6
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "GALAXY-S25",
  "name": "Samsung Galaxy S25 Ultra",
  "description": "Android smartphone, 512GB",
  "price": 109999.00
}

### Delete it → expect 204 No Content
DELETE {{host}}/api/products/6


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Failure cases. These are the interesting ones — run every single one and
#  read the response body. Knowing what your API does when things go wrong is
#  worth more than knowing what it does when they go right.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 404 — no such id
GET {{host}}/api/products/9999

### 404 — no such SKU
GET {{host}}/api/products/sku/DOES-NOT-EXIST

### 400 — id is not a number, so binding fails before the controller runs
GET {{host}}/api/products/abc

### 400 — three constraint violations at once, reported per field
POST {{host}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "lowercase-not-allowed",
  "name": "   ",
  "price": -100.00
}

### 400 — price has more decimal places than NUMERIC(12,2) can hold
POST {{host}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "TOO-PRECISE",
  "name": "Overly precise product",
  "price": 12.3456
}

### 400 — required fields missing entirely
POST {{host}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "no sku, no name, no price"
}

### 400 — malformed JSON
POST {{host}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{ not actually json

### 409 — SKU already exists (run twice: first 201, then 409)
POST {{host}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "CONFLICT-TEST",
  "name": "Conflict test",
  "price": 100.00
}

### 404 — deleting something that is not there is honest about it
DELETE {{host}}/api/products/9999
